      "created_at": "2016-02-04T22:32:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>We have a previous ruling that it still counts as a power use.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Using Prejudice via the text on Pride counts as a power use. For example, play Embolden on Expatriette. On her turn, use Pride, then use Prejudice as part of that. You have now used two powers, and you’re done. If you were clever and used Prejudice first, then you could use Pride and trigger Prejudice a second time.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/clarifications-and-decisions-from-handelabra-christophers-fireside-chats-6773\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Fireside chats</a></p>",
